commands.descr:
The same goods CmdList walks, narrowed by a query written as json.

ASKED FOR NOTHING - an empty query, or none at all - it answers its own signature instead: the columns of a goods and the type of each, and what may be asked of them. Nothing outside that list is taken.

THE SHAPE. A query starts from the root table of the sign and holds a list of conditions. A list is an AND, always. Three things may stand in it:
a condition - {"field": "name", "op": "like", "value": "Bosch"};
an or - {"or": [ ..., ... ]};
a not - {"not": ...}, of one condition.
Nothing nests here: a goods hanging nowhere has no sections, and the rest of what hangs on it belongs to the other tools of the Goods branch.

BESIDE THE ROOT TABLE nothing stands. The page is a field of the call - limit and offset - and the goods come by id. Whatever the page, the answer carries found, the whole count of what matched.

THE OPERATIONS come from the type of the column, and the sign names them: eq, in for the id, eq, in, like for words. like looks for a part of the text anywhere in it.

AN EXAMPLE:
{"store": [
  {"or": [ {"field": "name", "op": "like", "value": "Bosch"},
            {"field": "code_shop", "op": "like", "value": "F-0"} ]}
]}

The goods of a list of ids are asked for the same way: {"store": [ {"field": "id", "op": "in", "value": [25, 26]} ]}.
